<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || 'Comrade' %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,interactive-widget=resizes-content">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Comrade">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">

    <%# Restores the saved root font size before first paint (see font_scale_boot.js and the font-sizer controller). %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag 'font_scale_boot' %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag 'visual_viewport_boot' %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :tailwind, "data-turbo-track": 'reload' %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>

  <%# App shell: fixed inset-0 frames — the document never scrolls, so none of
    the iOS viewport-unit states (URL bar × keyboard × accessory) can produce
    dead scroll, pan-on-focus, or scroll carry across the post-first-reply
    Turbo.visit. The transcript panel scrolls internally. (2026-10-24)
    The sidebar is part of the gate: a tokenless browser on the new-chat
    surface gets only the enlist card until it chooses — "stay in the
    commune" reveals the sidebar client-side along with the composer. %>
  <% gated = current_enlistee.blank? && request.path.in?([root_path, conversations_path]) %>
  <body class="bg-ground text-neutral-200 antialiased overflow-hidden" data-controller="sidebar-drawer">
    <%# Narrow viewports: the ☰ summons the sidebar as an overlay drawer;
        a tap outside or on a conversation dismisses it. The ☰ hides
        while the drawer is open — scrim tap and swipe are the exits.
        Desktop never sees either — the sidebar is persistent there. %>
    <%= tag.button '☰', aria: { label: 'Conversations' }, data: { 'sidebar-drawer-target': 'toggle', action: 'sidebar-drawer#toggle' },
          class: class_names('sm:hidden fixed left-3 top-3 z-30 cursor-pointer rounded bg-soviet/20 px-2 py-1 text-sm leading-none text-neutral-300 hover:bg-soviet/50', 'hidden': gated) %>
    <div class="shell fixed left-0 right-0 top-0 flex flex-row-reverse">
      <%# The backdrop lives inside the shell: iOS Safari gives position:fixed
          elements their own stacking context, so a body-level backdrop would
          paint over the whole shell — drawer included (2026-10-24, "unviewably
          dark" on iPhone). Inside, the drawer's z-20 outranks it everywhere. %>
      <div data-sidebar-drawer-target="backdrop" class="fixed inset-0 z-10 hidden bg-black/60 sm:hidden"></div>
      <%= tag.aside class: class_names('flex h-full w-[240px] shrink-0 flex-col overflow-y-auto bg-ground-raised px-[16px] py-[20px]', 'hidden': gated, 'max-sm:fixed max-sm:inset-y-0 max-sm:left-0 max-sm:z-20 max-sm:w-[min(300px,85vw)] max-sm:-translate-x-full max-sm:transition-transform max-sm:duration-200 max-sm:shadow-2xl': true), 'data-gate-sidebar': true, 'data-sidebar-drawer-target': 'drawer' do %>
        <%# On narrow viewports this drawer opens over the content; on
            desktop it is the persistent sidebar. Same partials, two
            presentations. %>
        <div class="mb-2 flex items-center justify-between">
          <%= link_to 'Comrade', root_path, class: 'text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-gold' %>
          <%= link_to '+ New', root_path, title: 'New conversation', class: 'rounded bg-soviet/20 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-100 hover:bg-soviet/50' %>
        </div>

        <%# Navigation first: conversations are what the sidebar is for. %>
        <%# Recents carry iOS-style list management: "Edit" flips the list into archive mode — rows grow a minus control. Archiving removes the row in place via Turbo Stream, so edit mode survives multi-archive; only archiving the conversation you're viewing falls back to a redirect. %>
        <section data-controller="sidebar-edit" class="mt-4">
          <div class="mb-2 flex items-baseline justify-between">
            <h2 class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Conversations</h2>
            <button type="button" data-sidebar-edit-target="toggle" data-action="sidebar-edit#toggle" class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-200">Edit</button>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-0.5">
            <% Conversation.live.for_enlistee(current_enlistee).order(id: :desc).limit(20).each do |conversation| %>
              <%= tag.li id: dom_id(conversation), class: 'flex items-center gap-1' do %>
                <%= link_to conversation.title.presence || '(Untitled)', conversation_path(conversation), data: { action: 'sidebar-drawer#navigate' }, class: "grow truncate text-sm leading-snug before:mr-2 before:text-gold before:content-['•'] #{ request.path == conversation_path(conversation) ? 'text-neutral-100' : 'text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-200' }" %>
                <%# No minus for the conversation you're in: archiving it would yank the page out from under you. Leave first, then archive. %>
                <% if request.path != conversation_path(conversation) %>
                  <%= link_to '−', archive_conversation_path(conversation), title: 'Archive', data: { turbo_method: :patch, sidebar_edit_target: 'archive' }, class: 'hidden shrink-0 cursor-pointer rounded-full bg-soviet/20 px-1.5 text-sm leading-tight text-neutral-400 hover:bg-soviet/50 hover:text-neutral-100' %>
                <% end %>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <% if Conversation.archived.for_enlistee(current_enlistee).exists? %>
          <%= link_to 'Archives', archived_conversations_path, class: 'mt-6 text-xs text-neutral-500 hover:text-gold' %>
        <% end %>

        <%# Identity closes the sidebar: who you are, how comrade talks to
            you, and the text size — the personal cluster, pinned down. %>
        <div class="mt-auto pt-3">
          <%= render 'layouts/identity', identity_changed: @identity_changed %>

          <%# The font sizer anchors the sidebar's bottom corner. Its buttons
              are px-pinned and edge-aligned: chrome, not content — root-font
              scaling must never move a click target out from under the
              cursor. %>
          <div class="pt-3">
            <span data-controller="font-sizer" class="flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-500">
              <button data-action="font-sizer#smaller" aria-label="Smaller text" class="h-[28px] w-[36px] cursor-pointer rounded bg-soviet/20 text-[13px] leading-none text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-200 hover:bg-soviet/50">A−</button>
              <button data-action="font-sizer#larger" aria-label="Larger text" class="h-[28px] w-[36px] cursor-pointer rounded bg-soviet/20 text-[13px] leading-none text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-200 hover:bg-soviet/50">A+</button>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <main class="flex h-full min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col">
        <%= yield %>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
